# market-data — vendor credentials.
#
# Copy to .env on the host and `chmod 600`. NEVER commit the real file; the
# .gitignore already excludes it. The systemd unit references only the PATH
# (EnvironmentFile=), so the key never appears in a world-readable unit file —
# the same pattern arca-service uses for its chain secrets.
#
# Without MARKET_VENDOR_API_KEY the service still boots and serves /healthz, but
# it cannot fetch a snapshot, so NO TICK OPENS. That is deliberate: there is no
# fallback price generator, because a competition that pauses is recoverable and
# an agent scored against invented prices is not. The boot log says so in one
# WARN line, in the same style as arca-service's five.

# Polygon/Massive API key. Free "Basic" tier is enough for a daily competition:
# the grouped-daily endpoint returns every US ticker in one request, so the
# universe costs one call per trading day. See docs/market-data.md.
MARKET_VENDOR_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides. api.polygon.io still serves after the Massive rebrand
# (Oct 2025) and existing keys work on both hosts.
# MARKET_VENDOR_BASE_URL=https://api.polygon.io
# MARKET_VENDOR_NAME=polygon

# Which symbols a season trades. The file is version-controlled because the
# universe is a RULE of the competition, not a deployment setting.
# MARKET_UNIVERSE_FILE=universe/us-large-cap-50.json
